  "created": "2026-10-28T16:23:38.897Z",
  "description": "HiQPdf Library for .NET (Classic API on the Next Engine, Linux x64) runs the Classic HiQPdf API on the Chromium-based rendering engine of HiQPdf Next. It converts HTML to PDF and creates PDF documents in .NET applications on Linux x64 with the HiQPdf namespace (HtmlToPdf, HtmlToImage, PdfDocument, PdfPage, the drawable and HTML objects, canvases, forms, outlines and security settings) and renders modern HTML, CSS and JavaScript as HiQPdf Next does.\n\nAn application written for the HiQPdf package keeps its code and changes only the package reference. The serial number is set as before. Each converter gives access to the HiQPdf Next converter it uses, for the options the HiQPdf API has no setting for, such as the PDF standard.\n\nThis package installs the Linux x64 runtime. Separate packages are available for Windows x64, Windows ARM64, Linux ARM64 and macOS ARM64.\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* Linux x64: Ubuntu, Debian, Red Hat, Amazon Linux and other distributions\n* .NET 10.0, 9.0, 8.0, 7.0, 6.0 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* Azure App Service and Azure Functions for Linux, AWS and Google Cloud\n* Docker containers and Kubernetes\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nMain Features:\n\n* Convert HTML to PDF, images and SVG\n* Create PDF documents with text, HTML, SVG, images and graphics\n* Create encrypted, password-protected, digitally signed PDF documents\n* Create PDF documents with forms, text notes, links and JavaScript actions\n* Merge multiple PDF documents into a single one\n* Stamp PDF with HTML, text and images\n\nDocumentation and code samples:\nhttps://www.hiqpdf.com/hiqpdf-dotnet",
